{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904008-would-the-solars-have-created-new-dragon-kings-if-they-could-have","id":904008,"title":"Would the Solars have created new Dragon Kings if they could have?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-31T00:31:12-07:00","id":904008,"title":"Would the Solars have created new Dragon Kings if they could have?","content":"We know it is possible to create new Mountain Folk, so it makes you wonder why the Solars never tried to restore the numbers of the Dragon Kings. Assuming it was in their power, why do you think they didn't? Is it just to reinforce the &quot;tragic, fallen heroes of yesterday&quot; vibe they have going, or do you think there are good, in-game reasons for why there numbers weren't increased?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T01:10:58-07:00","id":904027,"title":"","content":"The problem in 2nd ed was that the Dragon Kings lost many of their souls during the Primordial war, and thus couldn't rebuild their population. Even if new souls could be made, they wouldn't be as powerful, as Dragon Kings got a lot of their power from their memories of past lives, so the amount of effort the Solars would have put in wouldn't give that much short term profit.<br /> <br /> Also Solars probably didn't trust an entire civilization of high powered dinosaur people. Look what they did to other races during the early First Age, the Dragon Kings were only spared due to their shared Loyalty to the Unconquered Sun and their choice of fighting against the Primordials in the Primordial war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T01:38:41-07:00","id":904041,"title":"","content":"Setting wise its best that the Solars didn't increase there numbers, it illustrates a costs of the primordial war, great civilization laid low and all that.<br /> <br /> In terms of the returned Solars there isn't any reason why they couldn't create more souls for them and have then start the process of gaining memories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2325-builder","name":"Builder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T04:09:51-07:00","id":904078,"title":"","content":"Several factors in play:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1) Define &quot;possible&quot;. If it was sufficiently hard, they might not have done it (/done it YET).<br /> <br /> 2) Perhaps some tried, but the Host was hardly unified; perhaps the wrong people were the only ones to take a stab at it.<br /> <br /> 3) Perhaps the DK's didn't really want more souls, they wanted the dead back, not new people; semi-immortals have a different perspective on things?<br /> <br /> 4) Perhaps they DID do it. Once. Right before Calibration....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T05:27:28-07:00","id":904097,"title":"","content":"I wonder if it's the sort of thing that they might go &quot;oh, wouldn't it be nice if we could make more&quot; but no-one was willing to do the kind of massive Solar workings necessary, because in a way... they <i>didn't</i> want to make more Dragon King souls.<br /> <br /> See, they obviously had to say &quot;Oh, we love Dragon Kings, they were our good allies&quot;, but Solars were humans, and it was convenient for them to not have many DKs left. They could put them in some out-of-the-way areas that humans didn't want and not worry about them too much. The Solars wanted a world of humans. The fact the DKs shared the same religion as them wasn't enough to want to share the world with them. Enough that they wouldn't, say, massacre or drive out the DKs, but not enough that they'd want to reivigorate a race that once oversaw humanity, a race far more powerful than humans.<br /> Oh, Solar poets might write paens to the lost glory of the Dragon Kings, Solar historians write books extolling the virtues of ancient DK civilisation, but if someone suggested actually letting the DKs produce more kids... oh dear, the sorcerers would explain, that's just not practical. No, no. The metaphysical soul-forging integration matrixes just won't align. No, no, can't be done. But how about this working to create a massive island of greenery in the snowy wasters of the North, for human settlers to live in? Yes, that can definitely be done.<br /> <br /> It's like how western newspapers and commentators will decry how terrible things are in Syria, people and governments will donate money to those poor, starving refugees, but share our country with them? No, no, that's just not practical. No, they should stay over there.<br /> <br /> I mean, Builder is right about the OOC reason. But I think that's a possible IC reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T08:50:02-07:00","id":904200,"title":"","content":"I agree with Wiz that it's unlikely the Exalted would be inclined to make competition for themselves. People are generally willing to help those in need or their allies, in some cases pretty far.<br /> <br /> They normally do not, however act directly counter to their own long-term interests. It's one thing to give a homeless person your leftover sandwich and a $20. It's another to let them live in your spare bedroom for six months.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T09:57:41-07:00","id":904233,"title":"","content":"Let's not forget that prior to the Primordial War, humanity was the Dragon King's slave race. There was probably still some hard feelings about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T10:33:24-07:00","id":904259,"title":"","content":"Some would. Some wouldn't. Who are &quot;the Solars&quot;?<br /> <br /> It's like, what kind of America did &quot;the Founding Fathers&quot; want? You kind of need to get down to the individual personas and political blocs to get an answer to that question, which will amount to several answers alongside &quot;and this is how they argued about it&quot;.\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Define &quot;possible&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> There's that as well; are we talking strictly in terms of it being a physical possibility, or something within ready reach? Are there expenses? Are there questions of where necessary resources are going to come from? About where these extra Dragon Kings are going to live? Who is going to have responsibility; is that the kind of thing they're going to try to dodge, or jockey over being given?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-31-2016, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T11:21:20-07:00","id":904309,"title":"","content":"I think they would have, if they could have, once all the debate and argument hashed out. I don't really feel they'd have generally considered the Dragon Kings a threat. The First Age Solars I would view as on balance tending more towards arrogance or hubris.<br /> <br /> (By which I mean, I wouldn't credit them with on the average taking seriously that they even could be threatened. If anything I'd view them as tending towards being much like a lot like some people in modern Western democracies (people few in number, loud in voice). People supremacistic in their view of their own society and history, and in its capacity to absorb and persuade everyone to their worldview (to them the self evident fruit and pinnacle of rational progress to freedom desired by all humanity, except a few knuckle-draggers among their own society to be showered with contempt). People for whom it just isn't thinkable that any of the folk they are urging to be included and absorbed and shared with could ever disagree with their fundamental ideas of what society should be, could have some sense that they are a distinct people apart with their own leadership and loyalty and who might stand apart from a common idea of society indefinitely.)<br /> <br /> In the median high First Age Solar view, I'd imagine, Solar led civilization will conquer all, and all under Heaven can be included, absorbed and led by the natural elite. Why fear resurgent Dragon Kings? They'll obviously get with the Solar program. Speculatively, look at the kind of complacency, in thinking that they couldn't possibly be threatened, with the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> So I imagine that it's that the Solars they just couldn't make more souls, any more than they could replace the singular and imperishable behemoths forged in the world's dawn, when those were slain and lost. Magic, at least in 3e, is an art, and the conditions and inspiration cannot be reproduced where they are lacking. Being able to make a thing as grand as a Dragon King soul, and give life to a being as grand as Dragon King, yes, yet unable to control conditions so well they can make that specific things.<br /> <br /> (If not that, they were likely busy with other projects.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:27:51-07:00","id":904447,"title":"","content":"Maybe something went wrong. Most Exalts had no interest in restoring the dominion of their former slavemasters, but a few did, and they started a grand project. Unfortunately, the first few prototype souls were...well, the project was shuttered pretty quickly after the world got a look at those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T23:36:08-07:00","id":906248,"title":"","content":"Maybe they simply didn't care. Maybe the Dragon Kings asked them not too. Maybe they couldn't, because they weren't PCs.<br /> <br /> There are lots of things that have happened in the Exalted world that would have been different if it had been done by &quot;me&quot; or &quot;you&quot; or &quot;you&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11910-wick-black","name":"Wick Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T00:36:31-07:00","id":906266,"title":"","content":"I tend to think that opinions would have depended more on the age of the Exalt, younger exalts would probably decry putting any serious effort into an outdated people and probably just find DKs to be of little worth beyond a historical footnote and a vacation spot. It would probably be the elder Exalts that felt any strong feeling about them with a few youths who had particularly strong memories from past lives, these ancients were probably strong enough politically to do something but probably canceled out each others efforts or had other things going on that they were more interested in.<br /> All in all the Solar attitude regarding DKs was probably best described as 'out of sight, out of mind' with the average Solar not really caring much one way or the other and considering that the Solar's were probably consumed by their hobbies, Lunar's were off running experiments and Sidereals have an allergy to revisiting past decisions it was probably not even a particularly interesting idea much less an actual movement.<br /> On another note it would also probably offend the sensibilities of the Celestials to waste their time rebuilding what someone else already made instead of making something original since it implies that the designer was better than them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T06:28:44-07:00","id":906366,"title":"","content":"I think part of it is a definitional thing. The Dragon Kings were immortal souls crafted at the behest of the Primordals, and empowered by countless lifetimes of memories. Even if a Solar were to create something indistinguishable from a Dragon King, it wouldn't BE a Dragon King. To understand this, imagine two identical Carcano Model 91/38 carbines. One was used to assassinate president Kennedy in 1963. The other was not. One is a major historical artifact. The other is moderately priced deal at a gun show.<br /> <br /> If the Solars were to create new Dragon Kings, those creations would not be accepted as part of a Dragon king society where friendships and organizations last through series of incarnations. They would be instead perceived as an attempt to replace the deposed rulers of mankind with something which owes its existence to humans. This is just my headcanon, but I think it makes sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11828-ikari-gendo","name":"Ikari Gendo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11828_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T06:56:28-07:00","id":906382,"title":"","content":"I imagine that's what the Dragon Kings said. Elder Solars had strong social charms and could easily remind the Dragon Kings that they needed more people if their civilization was to grow, and the Dragon King charm set doesn't build itself up for mental defence to resist such influence. More likely the Solars just didn't want more Dragon kings interferrering with their new world","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T11:32:38-07:00","id":906584,"title":"","content":"Maybe they did.<br /> <br /> Let's assume that, say, about 500 years before the Usurpation, the Twilight Caste Glorious Violet Banner developed a sorcerous artifact that creates a new Dragon King soul every week. It has been in continuous operation ever since then.<br /> <br /> Well, then. The circa 125,000 new Dragon King souls so created to date are just a rounding error compared to the approximately 30 million Dragon King souls that survived the Primordial War or even the 4 million that survived the Great Contagion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T11:42:06-07:00","id":906595,"title":"","content":"First Age solars didn't bother with anything that was obsolete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}